* LD4_model.lib -- three interchangeable implementations of the same
* LD4_MODEL subckt (same name + pin interface in every section):
*   ideal  : single ideal inductor (unchanged, see its own section below)
*   rl     : EM-derived series L+R, L=8.4824n R=30.2594ohm (refreshed to the
*            currently-installed real coil, see EM_Flow/LD4/ for the
*            sim scripts + .s1p this was fitted from)
*   snp2le : snp2le broadband vector-fitted macromodel (same EM data as rl),
*            single-ended (port 2 forced to ground, matching the real
*            guard-ring short used in the EM simulation itself -- NOT a
*            true 2-port fit)
* Select the active one from the including file via:
*   .lib <path>/LD4_model.lib ideal   (or rl, or snp2le)

.lib ideal
.SUBCKT LD4_MODEL p1 p2
L1 p1 p2 8.44n
.ENDS LD4_MODEL
.endl ideal

.lib rl
.SUBCKT LD4_MODEL p1 p2
R1 p1 mid_LD4 30.2594
L1 mid_LD4 p2 8.4824n
.ENDS LD4_MODEL
.endl rl

.lib snp2le
.SUBCKT LD4_MODEL p1 p2
* ld4_fresh_snp2le - lumped-element equivalent (Ngspice / SPICE3)
* generated by snp2le 0.1.18
* EQUIVALENT CIRCUIT FOR VECTOR FITTED S-MATRIX
* Created using scikit-rf vectorFitting.py
* 
* 
* thermal noise of the passive: kT(I - S S^H) at the ports, from a spectral factor of this fit
* sources Rnz_e1..Rnz_e1 (0.25 ohm, the only noisy elements), 4 states nz_x*, controlled sources Gnz_*
* DC pin: Y = Y_fit + dY / (1 + s/wc), fc = 160 Hz, so the model meets the file's 0 Hz point. Nodes dcp_d*, controlled sources Gdcp_*, noiseless
V1 p1 s1 0.0
R1 s1 0 50.0 noisy=0
Gd1_1 0 s1 p1 0 0.007053608149934735
Fd1_1 0 s1 V1 0.35268040749673674
Gr1_1_1 0 s1 x1_a1 0 -1.2194811166560087
